# A shell script with CRLF line endings is not a shell script: dash reads
# "set -eu\r" as an illegal option and exits before the first line runs. The
# game-scheduler entrypoint is executed straight from the working tree (the
# container bind-mounts ./backend), so a checkout that rewrote its line
# endings would leave the sidecar unable to start -- silently, because the
# container's command is the script itself.
#
# Every shell script is therefore stored and checked out with LF endings,
# whatever the host's core.autocrlf says.
*.sh text eol=lf
